# Rust
/target/
# Alternate target dirs. Default-features and `--no-default-features` builds MUST NOT share one:
# proven to make a test shell out to the wrong binary and report a false green.
/target-*/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# NOTE: Cargo.lock IS committed for binaries (busbar is a bin) — do not ignore it.

# Local runtime config & secrets (real config is mounted; keys come from env)
config.json
*.env
.env
.env.*

# Editor / IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs / scratch
*.log
/scratch/

# Stray debug/scratch artifacts (never commit)
/rust_out
/scratch_syms.txt

# Signing keys generated locally during plugin-sign testing (never commit)
*.key

# Python bytecode (bench harness)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.wrangler/

# SQLite dev/test artifacts left in a crate root by a plugin's own default relative db_path
# (e.g. crates/plugin-loader's store-sqlite-plugin fixture tests before they were isolated to a
# tmpdir) — never something to commit.
busbar-governance.db

# cargo-mutants report output pulled from EC2 shards (scripts/run-mutants-ec2.sh) — local
# working data, not source.
mutants-report/
mutants-report-live/

# proptest writes a regression seed file here when a property fails. It is a debugging aid for the
# person looking at the failure, not source, and CI now asserts the working tree is CLEAN after the
# full suite. Untracked, a failing proptest would trip that assertion TOO, so one flake reports as
# two failures and the second points at the wrong thing entirely.
crates/*/proptest-regressions/

# MCP conformance scratch: the pinned third-party control peer's checkout and every run's results.
# Both are outputs of `scripts/mcp-conformance.sh`, rebuilt from a pin on every run, and a committed
# results directory is worse than none — a gate that falls back to a stale report is a gate that
# reports a state it never reached.
/.mcp-conformance/
/.sdk-under-test/
